From 354e2b444a6a032bd32d5672f0a36b894f99bf8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:30:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lumen tools, light theme: the gold accent reads at 4.5:1 or
 more (needs the author's approval)

In the light theme a tool's accent (labels, links, ghost buttons, focus) is its family colour mixed with near black;
for Lumen's gold at 62% that is #9c824a: 3.18:1 on a grey row and 3.68:1 on white, too little for small text (axe:
151 nodes on 9 Lumen tools, among them the 8D report's D7 buttons in every language). At 48% it is #7b683e: 4.67:1
and 5.40:1, and all of them pass (tools-scan.txt before, tools-scan-after-lumen.txt after). The planet, the sky and
the dark theme are unchanged; the gold text is a shade deeper (before and after images in
docs/audit/2026-10-27/phase3/ci-a11y/). A visible change of a family colour: kept apart so it can be dropped, and
then the a11y suite's KNOWN list takes back the 8D entry (see the previous commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
